  "question": {
    "text": "When an $A C$ source of emf $E$ with frequency $\\omega=100 \\mathrm{~Hz}$ is connected across a circuit, the phase difference between\n$E$ and current I in the circuit is observed to be $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ as shown in the figure. If the circuit consist of only $\\mathrm{RC}$ or $\\mathrm{RL}$ in series, then\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/scgDMvLRCTaVROqZhcXm5lhCPNUh-IIFfpUDwYZCARI.original.fullsize.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "eNTsH",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{R}=1 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega, \\mathrm{C}=5 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
