      "text": "$\\mathrm{R}=1 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega, \\mathrm{L}=1 \\mathrm{H}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7p9C7",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{R}=1 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega, \\mathrm{C}=10 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": ".. Since supply voltage lags the current $\\operatorname{By}(\\phi=\\pi / 4)$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\tan \\phi=\\frac{\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{C}}}{\\mathrm{R}}=1, \\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{C}}=\\mathrm{R} \\ldots \\ldots(1) \\\\\n&\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{C}}=\\frac{1}{\\omega \\mathrm{C}}=\\frac{1}{100 \\times 10 \\times 10^{-6}}=1 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega=\\mathrm{R}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
